-- title:
--   Theorem 4.2, p. 1489 — under the uniform ℙ, μ is a distortion risk measure iff μ(X) = −Σ qᵢ x₍ᵢ₎ for some q ∈ Δ̂ᴺ; every such q mixes the CVaR_{j/N} generators q̂ʲ
-- statement:
--   Let $\Omega = \{\omega_1, \dots, \omega_N\}$, $N \ge 1$, carry the uniform distribution (Assumption 4.1), and let $\mu : \mathbb R^N \to \mathbb R$ be a risk measure. For $j = 1, \dots, N$ let $\hat q^j \in \mathbb R^N$ have entries $1/j$ in its first $j$ coordinates and $0$ elsewhere.
--
--   1. $\mu$ is a distortion risk measure if and only if there is $q \in \hat\Delta^N$ such that
--   $$\mu(X) = -\sum_{i=1}^N q_i x_{(i)} \qquad \text{for all } X \in \mathbb R^N, \tag{4}$$
--   where $x_{(1)} \le \cdots \le x_{(N)}$ are the increasing order statistics of $X$.
--   2. Every $q \in \hat\Delta^N$ can be written as
--   $$q = \sum_{j=1}^N \lambda_j \hat q^j, \qquad \lambda \ge 0,\ \sum_{j=1}^N \lambda_j = 1. \tag{5}$$
--   3. Each $\hat q^j$ lies in $\hat\Delta^N$ and corresponds to $\mathrm{CVaR}_{j/N}$: $\mathrm{CVaR}_{j/N}(X) = -\sum_i \hat q^j_i x_{(i)}$ for all $X$.
--
--   So distortion risk measures on a uniform finite space are exactly the measures (4) with nonincreasing weights, and they are finitely generated by the $N$ measures $\mathrm{CVaR}_{1/N}, \dots, \mathrm{CVaR}_{N/N}$.
--
--   **Formalization Note** Indices are 0-based: `qhat j` for `j : Fin N` is the paper's $\hat q^{j+1}$, and part 3 reads $\mathrm{CVaR}_{(j+1)/N}$. The page's (5) writes $\sum_{i=1}^N \lambda_j \hat q^j$; the sum is over $j$. "$\hat q^j$ corresponds to the distortion risk measure $\mathrm{CVaR}_{j/N}$" is stated as the identity $\mathrm{CVaR}_{j/N} = \mu_{\hat q^j}$ under the uniform distribution. The hypothesis "$\mu$ is a risk measure" is kept as on the page; it is not strengthened to coherence.
-- source:
--   Bertsimas & Brown, Constructing uncertainty sets for robust linear optimization, Oper. Res. 57(6) (2009), p. 1489, Theorem 4.2, displays (4), (5); Definition 4.6, p. 1489

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_RiskUncSets_Distortion_Setting

namespace RiskUncSets.Distortion

theorem theorem_4_2 {N : ℕ} (hN : 0 < N) (μ : (Fin N → ℝ) → ℝ) (hμ : IsRiskMeasure μ) :
    (IsDistortion (uniform N) μ ↔ ∃ q ∈ restrictedSimplex N, ∀ X, μ X = muQ q X) ∧
      (∀ q ∈ restrictedSimplex N, ∃ lam : Fin N → ℝ, (∀ j, 0 ≤ lam j) ∧ ∑ j, lam j = 1 ∧
        q = ∑ j, lam j • qhat j) ∧
      (∀ j : Fin N, qhat j ∈ restrictedSimplex N ∧
        ∀ X, cvar (uniform N) (((j : ℕ) + 1 : ℝ) / N) X = muQ (qhat j) X) := by sorry

end RiskUncSets.Distortion
